      "id": "hcy72y0",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Constitutional Articles Related to President"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The President is elected indirectly by an Electoral College comprising elected members of both Houses of Parliament and State Legislative Assemblies (including Delhi and Puducherry).",
        "Qualifications require being a citizen of India, at least 35 years of age, and qualified for election as a member of the Lok Sabha.",
        "Article 61 outlines the impeachment process for 'violation of the Constitution', requiring a two-thirds majority of total membership in both Houses.",
        "The President holds Ordinance-making powers under Article 123 when Parliament is not in session.",
        "Judicial powers under Article 72 allow the President to grant pardons, reprieves, respites, or remissions of punishment."
      ],
      "id": "2ocb1l7"
    },
